      <slug></slug>
      <title>Automating installations</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>Debian</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Automating installations using preseeding in Debian Installer&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </abstract>
      <description>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;An introduction to how installing Debian can be automated using &amp;#34;preseeding&amp;#34;.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The talk will give some background information on how preseeding is basically just making use of the debconf protocol, which preseeding methods are available, and how to create a preconfiguration file. Some potential problems and current limitations of using preseeding will be discussed as well.&#xA;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA; </description>
      <persons>
          <person id="171">Frans Pop</person>
      </persons>
